---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Pace — company-wide skills for AI coding agents"
  description="One router, many commands across engineering, product, ops, and marketing. For design, pace defers to impeccable."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>pace</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Company-wide skills for AI coding agents. One router (<code>/pace</code>),
      many commands across engineering, product, ops, and marketing.
    </p>

    <p>
      For frontend design, pace defers to <a href="https://impeccable.style">impeccable</a>.
      The installer offers to bring it along.
    </p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <pre><code>npx pace skills install</code></pre>

    <h2>Use</h2>
    <pre><code>/pace &lt;command&gt; [target]</code></pre>

    <p class="status">
      Pace is in scaffold. Commands ship as they're authored.
      Track progress on <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/pace.tools">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose h1 {
    font-family: 'Instrument Sans', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .prose .lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: 'Instrument Sans', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .prose pre {
    background: var(--color-mist);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .prose code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.95em;
  }
  .prose .status {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
